// tests/kernel/drivers/usb/msc/hw_smoke_placeholder.pdx — R34.M3-005 (#1180)
//
// DORMANT hardware-gated placeholder.
//
// #1180 delivers `tools/hw-smoke-r34.md`: an operator recipe for
// exercising USB mass-storage mount + read + write against a real
// T14 G4 with a real USB flash key attached. Per design/roadmap/
// next-wave-synthesis.md §10 D7 (gated:hardware discipline), an
// issue whose acceptance requires PHYSICAL hardware in the loop
// CANNOT emit a golden fingerprint from a QEMU-OVMF boot -- the
// harness has no USB stick to enumerate, and the fingerprint would
// lie.
//
// The RIGHT SHAPE for a dormant issue is a placeholder module that
// COMPILES but emits NOTHING. This module is that placeholder. It
// carries no witness function, no fingerprint, and no boot-witness
// registration. The build-time coverage gate
// (tools/verify-fingerprint-coverage.sh) is satisfied because there
// is nothing to cover.
//
// When R34.M4 or a later milestone lands the USB flash smoke on
// real hardware, this file is replaced by a real synth that emits
// "MSC HW-SMOKE OK" and takes ITS marker into the golden.
//
// The empty module is deliberately unreferenced from
// r30_platform.pdx. That is the whole point of the dormant shape:
// nothing at boot calls into it, so nothing at boot lies about it.

module HwSmokePlaceholder = structure {
  // Compile-only marker so paideia-as accepts an "empty" module.
  pub let _r34_m3_005_hw_smoke_placeholder : u64 = 0
}
